  "content": {
    "id": "p49-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Find the percentage of the population within one standard deviation of the mean, to 2 s.f.:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p49-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=2x$, domain $[0,1]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$63\\%$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=\\int_0^1 x(2x)\\,dx\\\\E(X)&=\\left[\\frac{2x^3}{3}\\right]_0^1=\\frac23\\\\E(X^2)&=\\int_0^1 x^2(2x)\\,dx\\\\E(X^2)&=\\left[\\frac{x^4}{2}\\right]_0^1=\\frac12\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\frac12-\\left(\\frac23\\right)^2=\\frac1{18}\\\\\\sigma&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{6}\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\int_{(4-\\sqrt2)/6}^{(4+\\sqrt2)/6}2x\\,dx\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\left[x^2\\right]_{(4-\\sqrt2)/6}^{(4+\\sqrt2)/6}\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\frac{4\\sqrt2}{9}\\end{align*}$$\nPercentage $=\\dfrac{4\\sqrt2}{9}\\times100\\%\\approx63\\%$ (2 s.f.).",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p49-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=|x|$, domain $[-1,1]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$50\\%$",
          "worked": "The density is symmetric about $0$, so $\\mu=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X^2)&=\\int_{-1}^1 x^2|x|\\,dx\\\\E(X^2)&=2\\int_0^1 x^3\\,dx\\\\E(X^2)&=2\\left[\\frac{x^4}{4}\\right]_0^1=\\frac12\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\frac12-0^2=\\frac12\\\\\\sigma&=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\int_{-1/\\sqrt2}^{1/\\sqrt2}|x|\\,dx\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=2\\int_0^{1/\\sqrt2}x\\,dx\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\left[x^2\\right]_0^{1/\\sqrt2}=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nPercentage $=\\dfrac12\\times100\\%=50\\%$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 53
      },
      {
        "id": "p49-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{3}{64}x^2$, domain $[0,4]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$67\\%$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=\\int_0^4 x\\left(\\frac{3x^2}{64}\\right)\\,dx\\\\E(X)&=\\left[\\frac{3x^4}{256}\\right]_0^4=3\\\\E(X^2)&=\\int_0^4 x^2\\left(\\frac{3x^2}{64}\\right)\\,dx\\\\E(X^2)&=\\left[\\frac{3x^5}{320}\\right]_0^4=\\frac{48}{5}\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\frac{48}{5}-3^2=\\frac35\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac35}\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\int_{3-\\sqrt{3/5}}^{3+\\sqrt{3/5}}\\frac{3x^2}{64}\\,dx\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\left[\\frac{x^3}{64}\\right]_{3-\\sqrt{3/5}}^{3+\\sqrt{3/5}}\\\\P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)&=\\frac{69}{80}\\sqrt{\\frac35}\\end{align*}$$\nPercentage $=\\dfrac{69}{80}\\sqrt{\\dfrac35}\\times100\\%\\approx67\\%$ (2 s.f.).",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
